(Stage 1e2 - `is a map` predicate. A static map variable folds to true;
 a list is not a map; and a runtime-tagged value (a mixed-list element)
 is classified by its tag. Acceptance: the four lines below.)

a map called m is {"a": 1}.
a list called xs is [1, 2].
if m is a map, print "m is a map".
if xs is a map, print "xs is a map".
if xs is not a map, print "xs is not a map".
for each item in [{"a": 1}, 2]
  if item is a map, print "item is a map".
  otherwise print "item is not a map".